    "note": "A **customer** buys from a shop or a business (*a regular customer at the café*). A **client** pays a professional, such as a lawyer or a designer, for advice or a service, often over a long time. A **shopper** is someone who is shopping at the moment. A **consumer** is anyone who buys and uses goods, used especially when people talk about buying in general (*consumers are spending less*)."
  },
